{% extends 'layout.twig' %}

{% block body %}
  <div class="card help-page">
    <h2>Help</h2>
    <p class="lede">What each part of OSMHelper does, and how to use it. Pages fetch fresh data from Online Scout Manager when you open them, so some tools take a moment.</p>

    <section class="help-section" id="home">
      <h3>Home</h3>
      <p>After you sign in, Home (nav label for the signed-in hub at <code>/dashboard/</code>) shows your name and group, and shortcuts into the tools. The public home page at <code>/</code> explains the product and lets you connect with OSM.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="dashboard">
      <h3>Dashboard (group numbers)</h3>
      <p>Membership counts by section type (Beavers, Cubs, Scouts, and Squirrels when anyone of that age is on the waiting list). Shows leaders, capacity, spaces, and waiting subtotals. The header reconciles waiting-list size with <strong>Waiting of age</strong>, <strong>Squirrels</strong>, <strong>Too young</strong>, and <strong>Explorers / too old</strong>.</p>
      <p>At the top of the page, snapshot charts (same data as the tables, no extra OSM calls) show <strong>members vs spaces</strong> by section (including over capacity), <strong>waiting by age band</strong>, and <strong>fullness %</strong> by section type (sections without a set capacity are omitted). Labelled as of page load.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="members">
      <h3>Members</h3>
      <p>A flat list of youth and young leaders across your accessible sections, with age/DoB filled in where OSM needs an extra lookup. Use the section checkboxes to show or hide rows without reloading the page. The table is sortable, searchable, and exportable (CSV / Excel / PDF). Leaders are not listed here.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="checks">
      <h3>Checks</h3>
      <p>Troubleshooting tables: youth in more than one section (excluding Leaders and Young Leaders patrols), Young Leaders checks, and Leaders checks. Status cells use green for OK and amber for issues. Each table supports sort, search and export.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="waiting">
      <h3>Waiting</h3>
      <p>Pulls your OSM waiting list, scores ages against the cutoffs in Settings, and suggests ideal sections. Sort, search and export the table. An empty list can be normal if everyone has moved elsewhere (for example Scoutworks).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="equipment">
      <h3>Equipment</h3>
      <p>Quartermaster lists and items for the section you choose under Settings → Equipment. Pick the section that holds your kit (often Adults). Shows all OSM fields (name, quantity, description, condition, broken, location, purchase date, notes, renewal price). Rows with Broken &gt; 0 are highlighted. Select multiple items and move them to a location from Settings → Equipment locations. You always review the list before Confirm; OSMHelper then updates Location (column 3) via OSM’s <code>updateListItemColumnValue</code> (value=location), spaced ~150ms apart to stay rate-limit friendly. The table supports sort, search and export (CSV / Excel / PDF), same as Members, Checks and Waiting. If OSM blocks item detail for a list, the list names still show with a short note.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="bank">
      <h3>Bank</h3>
      <p>Lists bank accounts for the finance section you pick in Settings (active accounts by default; optional show deleted). Balances are OSM pence ÷ 100. Click an account to see transactions (date, reference, amount, type/transfer, description) via OSM’s v3 accounting API. Sort, search and export on both tables. Read-only — no bank writes.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="settings">
      <h3>Settings</h3>
      <p>Age cutoffs, capacity per section, which section Equipment uses, which section Bank uses, and a named <strong>Equipment locations</strong> list (add, edit, reorder, remove). Saves on this server (not only in your browser session) so they stick after logout. Locations power the Equipment bulk-move destination list.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="rate-limit">
      <h3>API rate limit</h3>
      <p>OSM applies an API allowance <strong>per user</strong> (your OSM login) — it is not a “how busy OSM is” meter. Home and the hub show your limit, remaining requests, and when the window resets. If remaining is low, open fewer heavy pages until it refreshes. Members, Checks, Dashboard, Waiting, Equipment and Bank each use quota when you load them.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="tables">
      <h3>Tables (sort, search, export)</h3>
      <p>On <strong>Members</strong>, <strong>Checks</strong>, <strong>Waiting</strong> and <strong>Equipment</strong>, click a column header to sort, use Search to filter rows, and export the visible rows as <strong>CSV</strong>, <strong>Excel</strong> (.xls), or <strong>PDF</strong> (opens the print dialog — choose Save as PDF). Data tables use gentle alternating row colours for readability.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="roadmap">
      <h3>Roadmap</h3>
      <p>See what is planned next on the <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap</a> page (phases P2–P4 and backlog).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="contact">
      <h3>Questions?</h3>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:jon@osmhelper.co.uk">jon@osmhelper.co.uk</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
